    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16541" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exaequātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		exaequo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an equalling.</i> * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>a levelling</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">agrorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Serv. Verg. G. 1, 95</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">concr.,</span>”
				<i>a level</i>, <i>a plane</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr.
					5, 12, 4</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>a levelling</i>, <i>an equality</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hanc ipsam exaequationem non fero (cf., shortly
					before: aequato omnium cultu),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					34, 4, 14</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
